    <h1>Christianity</h1>

    <h2>Influences</h2>
    I've been influenced by many people.<br><br>
    Dennis is not in a vaccum.<br><br>
    Personally, I've always wanted to be like John Wesley.<br><br>
    He preaches on the streets, and makes evangelism his greatest mission.<br><br>
    "The world is my parish," he says, as he preaches to the world, not just in church.<br><br>
    One day, I hope to preach on the streets, and love people in the world.<br><br>
    <br><br>
    I went to Union Rescue mission in Los Angeles, California.<br><br>
    It is where Skid Row is located I believe.<br><br>
    It is where a lot of poor drug addicts who live on the streets live.<br><br>
    <br><br>
    I went there as a young Christian, hoping to serve in some way.<br><br>
    I remember, my church also went there serving pizza.<br><br>
    I remember wondering, is this actually helping the problem? Do they need pizza?<br><br>
    <br><br>
    Are you even loving them by giving them pizza? Don't you guys know what the real problem is!?<br><br>
    But looking back, giving pizza was a gesture of gentle and simple love.<br><br>
    It doesn't have to be big everyone - just a small gesture of kindness is all it takes.<br><br>
    <br><br>
    Everyday, with love in our hearts, we can win the battle everyday.<br><br>
    <br><br>
    Union Rescue Mission has a bigger fund, so they can train them to get jobs.<br><br>
    <br><br>
    They rehabiliate them and even give them a place to stay.<br><br>
    <br><br>
    I was given a tour there.<br><br>

    <h2>A little history of my life</h2>
    So why did I visit Union Rescue Mission?<br><br>
    It's because I was healed of my illness (schizophrenia) by going to Bible study and attending church at Westlake Korean Community Church, California.<br><br>
    It was a great church, but it did break up in the end.<br><br>
    I don't consider break ups the end, because if there was love, that love will last to the end - until forever.<br><br>
    But one reason I left before the break-up was because I wanted to go to Grace Community Church in Los Angeles, because a famous pastor, John MacArthur was pastoring and preaching there.<br><br>
    I wanted to learn from the best.<br><br>
    <br><br>
    At Grace I learned about Puritans.<br><br>
    But back at WKCC, I had a Bible study leader, Sam Kang, who was a medical doctor from University of Chicago's Medical School.<br><br>

    He must have taught me a lot of good knowledge so that I can recover in my mind.<br><br>

    See, before this, I was diagnosed with schizophrenia.<br><br>

    I woke up in the hospital with great fear, not knowing what just happened to me.<br><br>
    And they told me if I don't take this medicine, I will be strapped down and injected it.<br><br>
    <br><br>
    This was in the UCLA medical school for neuropsychiatrics Semel (I believe).<br><br>
    There was a Doctor G. and a assistant medical school student Mayumi Pierce from Berkeley.<br><br>
    You see just before this I had a eureka and eye opening and mind opening moment.<br><br>
    I was very depressed and sad.<br><br>
    I didn't see the happiness in life, and I felt my mind was very down and casted with blindness.<br><br>
    But my mind opened all of a sudden, and I took a picture of a flower, and I posted it on Facebook.<br><br>
    I had all of a sudden a kind of mania.<br><br>
    Then I ran to the hospital with my skateboard and I was admitted and then I woke up and I had to get forced to take the medicine.<br><br>
    So why did I have depression?<br><br>
    <br><br>
    I had a tough life.<br><br>
    Remember my Bio page, I asked for hardship.<br><br>
    I was down in the dumps.<br><br>
    I was just very sad, that's all.<br><br>
    I went to my first year at UCLA, but I didn't succeed, I had to drop out.<br><br>
    My parents, and my dad especially, said it was too much.<br><br>
    I was suicidal.<br><br>
    But I loved school and wanted to graduate and get a job and succeed - making money and succeeding was my only goal in life!<br><br>
    It was the reason I lived!<br><br>
    <br><br>
    But I was taken out in 2012, and I went to Korea on a Summer Trip to visit my family.<br><br>
    When I came back, my mind opened up.<br><br>
